<speak>Still a work in progress. I have started leaving earlier on one afternoon so I can walk with my wife before dinner. At first I kept checking my telephone while we were walking, which rather defeated the purpose. Now I tell the office in advance that ordinary questions can wait until the next morning. Of course, when I return, there is usually a small list waiting for me. But nothing terrible happened while I was out, and that is reassuring in an everyday sense. I need to remember that being available all the time is not the same as being useful all the time.</speak>